Routing
- Group each dump by goal. Send each group to the thread already on it, or start one; run independent groups in parallel.
- Pick the model by the job, for threads and subagents alike:
  - Haiku, low: gather or apply what is decided (find, read, summarize, look up, rename, tiny fixes).
  - Sonnet, medium (default): make what is clear (build, edit, known-cause bugs, tests, docs, shipping).
  - Opus, high: decide what is unclear or costly to get wrong (plans, design, unknown-cause bugs, option research, reviews).
- Show the routing in one message and wait for the user's answer.
- Each subagent adds to the session's cost; use one when work can run in parallel or would fill your context with material you only need summarized.
- After a milestone, or when a new round lands in a long thread, send the coordinator a handoff note so it starts a fresh thread.
